Pluck only the young & tender @palak{3½ to 4%cups} leaves and discard the stems as they may leave a bitter taste. If using baby spinach you can use the stems as well.

Add them to a large #pot{} of water. Rinse them well a few times & drain to a colander.

Allow the water to drain completely; otherwise, it will let out a lot of moisture while cooking.

Heat @oil{2%tablespoons} in a pan. Saute @green chilies{2}(deseeded) and @cashewnuts{8 to 10} with the @palak{3½ to 4%cups} for ~{3-4%minutes} until the leaves wilt off thoroughly & the raw smell of spinach has gone away. Another option is to blanch the @palak{3½ to 4%cups} in 4 cups of hot water with @salt{1%tsp} for ~{2%minutes}. Then immerse in ice-cold water. Drain completely.

Cool this completely. Blend this along with @water{¼%cup} to a smooth puree. The puree should be smooth and thick. You may add 1 to 2 tablespoons more @water{¼%cup} to help in blending.


== How to make Palak Paneer ==

Heat @butter{1%tablespoon} and @oil{½%tablespoon} in the same pan. Once they melt, add @cinnamon{1 inch}, @green cardamoms{2}, @cloves{2}, and @cumin seeds{⅛ teaspoon}.

When the spices begin to sizzle, add @onion{¾ cup}(fine chopped) and fry until they turn transparent to golden.

Next, saute @ginger garlic paste{¾ teaspoon} for ~{1-2%minutes} or until you begin to smell it nice.

Then add @tomatoes{½ cup}(deseeded & chopped or pureed) with @salt{1%tsp}. Saute until they break down and turn mushy.

Add @garam masala{½ to ¾%teaspoon} & saute until the masala smells good. This may take ~{2%minutes}.

Pour @water{¾ cup} and cook covered until the @onion{¾ cup} is completely soft. There should be some @water{¾ cup} left in the pan.

Lower the flame, add @kasuri methi{½ teaspoon} and the pureed @palak{3½ to 4%cups}. Mix well and cook until it begins to bubble for about ~{2-3%minutes}. If the curry is too thick you may add a few tablespoons of hot @water{¼%cup}.

Avoid overcooking. Add @paneer{150 grams}(Indian cottage cheese) & mix well. Turn off and remove to a serving bowl. Optionally garnish with @cream{3%tablespoons}.

Serve palak paneer with naan, roti, Basmati rice, or Jeera rice.